# Orange demo environment variables.
# Copy to .env and fill in your values: cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is loaded automatically by `make run` / `make demo`.
# Format: KEY=value  (no export prefix, no shell substitution)

# ── Config file ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to orange.yaml (all providers). Use orange-no-env.yaml to run with
# only providers that need no API keys (Bedrock uses ambient AWS credentials).
#ORANGE_CONFIG=orange-no-env.yaml

# ── Provider credentials (required by orange.yaml) ──────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── GCP Vertex AI credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GCP_PROJECT: your GCP project ID (used by vertex + vertex_anthropic providers)
# GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON: raw value — no scheme prefix.
#   JSON content:  GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=$(cat my-sa-key.json)
#   File path:     GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=/path/to/key.json   (no file:// prefix)
# The env:// scheme is in orange.yaml's secret_ref, not here.
# Omit entirely to use Application Default Credentials (GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS,
# gcloud user creds, or Workload Identity).
GCP_PROJECT=
GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# ── AWS Bedrock credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by the bedrock provider. The SDK credential chain is tried in order:
# env vars below → ~/.aws/credentials → IAM instance/task role → etc.
# Omit all three to rely on ambient credentials (IAM role, AWS CLI profile).
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN is only needed for temporary credentials (STS AssumeRole).
# The region is set in orange.yaml (providers.bedrock.extra.region), not here.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
#AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# ── GitHub token (optional — MCP github server + e2e) ───────────────────────
# Needed only when the active config references env://GITHUB_TOKEN.
# Falls back to `gh auth token` in the e2e suite if unset.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ── MCP session encryption keys (optional) ───────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of base64 keys; first is primary, rest are fallback.
# Defaults to a static development key if unset (logs a warning).
# Use "orange-generated" to generate an ephemeral key on each restart.
#ORANGE_MCP_SESSION_KEYS=orange-generated

# ── Sidecar listen addresses (optional overrides) ────────────────────────────
# Default is ephemeral TCP (127.0.0.1:0 — OS picks a free port).
# Use a fixed port or a Unix domain socket for reproducible addresses.
#ORANGE_MCP_LISTEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:10004
#ORANGE_MCP_LISTEN_ADDR=unix:///tmp/orange-mcp.sock
#ORANGE_RESPONSESWS_LISTEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:10002
#ORANGE_RESPONSESWS_LISTEN_ADDR=unix:///tmp/orange-responsesws.sock
